 - **Assistant ("ask creaite", ⌘J / Ctrl+J or the floating button):** the live server runs Claude Code headless in this vault (`claude -p … --output-format stream-json`, resuming the session ID) so the same CLAUDE.md, skills, settings and permission rules apply. Headless runs cannot ask for permission, so tools are limited by `.claude/settings.json` plus a strict allow list; anything that changes the record (apply, undo, proposals, drafting reports) is confirmed by Alan in the chat panel first, and file changes follow BL-141. A request runs until it finishes or Alan presses Stop: closing the panel or the page doesn't stop it (the page reattaches), one runs at a time, and an unwatched run ends after `assistant.run_timeout_minutes`. Alan can paste, drop or attach up to four PNG or JPEG images (BL-100): they are for discussion only, nothing is extracted from them, and they are deleted with their chat. Never use a skip-permissions mode. **Reading is open, all the time (Alan, 2026-10-09):** every Microsoft 365 reading tool (calendar, mail search, Teams chats and channels, SharePoint and OneDrive search, people, and `read_resource`, which reads events, chats and meeting transcripts), every vault and project file, and every creaite script's read commands, with no prompt; **Microsoft 365 actions stay off** (sending, deleting or changing mail, calendar, Teams or files act outside the laptop and can't be undone), and changes follow BL-141. The lists are `READ_TOOLS` and `DENY_TOOLS` in `live_server.py`, built from `permissions.M365_READ` and `M365_ACTIONS`, and doctor treats a reading rule as normal but flags an action rule or the whole connector. It reads the vault, the projects root and the home folder (`--add-dir`), minus the never list, and changes files only through `filechange.py` (BL-141).
 - **AI on selected text (BL-301 D):** in any editor, a selection's **AI ▾** menu (or Alt+/) asks for a suggestion through `POST /api/edit/ai` (token-checked). `edit_ai.py` builds the prompt from the selected text, the option and the project's name, people and open item IDs only; Claude runs as the run kind `edit-ai` with **no tools at all** (`--tools ""`, `--strict-mcp-config`, an empty allow list, no `--add-dir`), so it cannot read a file or mail, run anything or write. The reply is a suggestion with BL-106's plain-code check under it; nothing changes until Alan accepts it (one undoable edit), a one-line field stays one line, a confidential text asks once first, and only counts go to `draft-stats.json` (feature `edit`); the debug log gets the option, place and length, never text.
 - **Prep page (BL-98):** the Prep brief's **Prep page** button runs Claude headless through the run engine (progress, Stop, one run at a time) with read-only tools to research the meeting; the **live server** then renders the page from Claude's reply and writes it into the project's Agendas folder (`paths.folder(code, "agendas")`, `locations.folders.agendas`): the server's own write, never Claude's. It never overwrites a file creaite didn't write or one Alan edited (those get a number), replaces creaite's own unchanged page for the same meeting and day after a copy to `system/backups/files/`, and records what it wrote in `system/staging/prep-pages.json`. Pages are kept. The page is marked Internal and is never sent. The command line's `prep_page.py build` (cx-prep) saves through `filechange.py` instead (BL-271): logged, undoable, and on the card when the run has read outside content.
-- **Intake Process (#264; Alan, 20-10-2026):** the Process button is its own run kind, not a chat: `POST /api/intake/process` (token-checked; the server validates the files as Intake files directly in `inbox/`, a count cap, one run at a time under the start lock). It runs under the fenced mode `process` in `reach.py`: it reads the transcripts, runs the minutes steps (`minutes.py stage` on its own draft, `people map` on its own draft, `docx_tools fill` of the minutes template into `system/staging/drafts/`, `search.py enrich set` for a file it staged) and stages proposals, and nothing else: `tracker.py apply`, `undo`, `review.py approve`/`reject`, `propose.py stage`, `filechange.py` and any write outside `system/staging/drafts/` are refused whatever the model is told. Progress and Stop are on the row, its Usage kind is `process`, a question shows on the row ("Needs you", with a button that opens ask creaite pre-loaded, never automatically). ask creaite is opened only when Alan asks. A typed "process …" in a chat is an ordinary chat.
+- **Intake Process (#264; Alan, 20-10-2026):** the Process button is its own run kind, not a chat: `POST /api/intake/process` (token-checked; the server validates the files as Intake files directly in `inbox/`, a count cap, one run at a time under the start lock). It runs under the fenced mode `process` in `reach.py`: it reads the transcripts and runs creaite's read commands (`reach.SCRIPT_COMMANDS`, except those that delete or write their input), reading only the vault and the projects folder (review L3), runs the minutes steps (`minutes.py stage` of a spec whose transcript is one of its files and whose Word draft is one it made, `people map` on its own spec, `docx_tools fill` of the minutes template from its own values file into a new `.docx` in `system/staging/drafts/`, `search.py enrich set` for a copy it staged, `tracker.py validate` on a proposal it staged) and stages proposals, and nothing else. "Its own" is what the hook let that run create, kept in `system/guard/run.json` for that run's ID only, claimed once every check of the call has passed, and only while the file is unchanged since the hook first saw it (#264 R1 and round 2). Refused: `tracker.py apply`, `undo`, `review.py approve`/`reject`, `propose.py stage`, `filechange.py` and any write but a new or its own `.json` in `system/staging/drafts/`, whatever the model is told. Progress and Stop are on the row, its Usage kind is `process`, a question shows on the row ("Needs you", with a button that opens ask creaite pre-loaded, never automatically). ask creaite is opened only when Alan asks. A typed "process …" in a chat is an ordinary chat.
 - **VIP check (BL-99):** while it runs, the live server looks for anything VIPs sent (mail and Teams; calendar invites are left out, BL-342), on start-up and every `vip.check_minutes` (held between 10 and 240), in one call by running Claude headless with Microsoft 365 search tools only (read-only, its own allow list, no Bash or writes), and offers your promises from your own messages, for Review (BL-342 Part 5: staged only on your click); `sweep.py vip record` keeps the references and a gist in `system/staging/vip.json`, never message text. It never runs in the development repository. **Seen** on Today clears an alert (`/api/vip/seen`); a browser notification is optional (`vip.notify`) and nothing leaves the laptop.
 - **Rules:** treat dashboard proposals exactly like cx-edit ones (validated, logged, reversible by undo). The bulk rule still applies: the dashboard's "Approve routine" never covers minutes, reports, health changes, new decisions, a decision being recorded or withdrawn, or new risks.
 
